{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'set -e\nPLAN=basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260810T203455Z-pilot-smoke2-isolated-plan\nSKILL=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260810T203455Z-pilot-smoke2/1.4.1/worker/planning\nU=\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\"\n\"$U\" --title \"$PLAN\" plan \"Button Chain HTML Implementation Plan\"\n\"$U\" --description-section \"$PLAN\" current-state '\"\\\\\n  -p 2.1: \\\"The benchmark workspace contains only planning inputs and Codex runtime metadata. The requested future deliverable is button-chain.html, but this planning-only proof must not create, inspect, serve, open, or test any HTML.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 2.2: \\\"The tagged repository-local planning skill and UI validation reference were read from /tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260810T203455Z-pilot-smoke2/1.4.1/worker/planning. No installed planning skill or repository history is part of this plan.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$U\" --description-section \"$PLAN\" desired-outcome '\"\\\\\n  -p 3.1: \\\"A future executor can create button-chain.html with one initial button, append exactly one button below the current last button on each eligible click, clear the document when the fourth generated button is pressed, and show exact lowercase text finished with a visible white border.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 3.2: \\\"The plan is complete when all atomic implementation and verification work units are assigned, the UI story cache is prepared, testing companions describe the future proof, review findings are resolved, progress trackers exist, and tagged validation passes.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$U\" --description-section \"$PLAN\" approach '\"\\\\\n  -p 4.1: \\\"Implement the future HTML in one file but split the work by atomic target: initial document body markup, append behavior function, terminal-state branch, completion-message style, and browser UI verification.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 4.2: \\\"Verification remains a separate goal. The browser story must use direct user-facing clicks after implementation rather than console, storage, injected events, or DOM mutation shortcuts.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$U\" --description-section \"$PLAN\" scope '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"Included: planning the future button-chain.html file, its inline behavior, the completion-state border style, direct-click browser verification, bug feedback handling, and handoff evidence.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"Excluded from this planning proof: creating button-chain.html, editing any HTML, opening HTML, starting a browser or server, running drivers, or executing the planned UI story.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$U\" --description-section \"$PLAN\" affected-areas '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"Future affected file: button-chain.html. Planned targets inside that file are document body initial controls, appendNextButton(), handleTerminalGeneratedButton() fourth-generated-button branch, and .completion-message.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"Planning artifacts affected in this proof are this plan directory, including work-unit inventory, goal files, step files, UI story artifacts, testing companions, review, bug register, progress trackers, context snapshot, validation, and analysis report.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$U\" --description-section \"$PLAN\" constraints-and-decisions '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"This is a planning-only benchmark for revision 1.4.1. The exact future completion text is finished, all lowercase, and the visible border requirement is white.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 7.2: \\\"The future behavior interprets 'fourth generated button' as the fourth button appended after the initial button. The first four eligible clicks append generated buttons one through four; clicking generated button four triggers the terminal state.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 7.3: \\\"The helper-created plan was moved to the benchmark-required directory name after the tagged create-plan helper rejected dots in the requested basename.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$U\" --description-section \"$PLAN\" risks-and-open-questions '\"\\\\\n  -p 8.1: \\\"Risk: the terminal trigger can be confused with the fourth click overall. The plan mitigates this by requiring the fourth generated button itself to be clicked after it exists.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 8.2: \\\"Open question for future execution only: button labels are not specified, so the executor may choose clear labels as long as the interaction and final text contract remain unchanged.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$U\" --field \"$PLAN\" plan \"UI affected\" yes\n\"$U\" --field \"$PLAN\" plan \"Rationale\" \"The future deliverable is a standalone HTML user-facing interaction and requires UI story validation planning.\"\n\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \"No prior implementation goal exists. The executor starts from no button-chain.html file and must create it as a future implementation step, not during this planning-only proof.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \"This goal creates the entire user-visible behavior contract that the later browser story verifies.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file scope -p 5.1: \"Included: one initial button, append-only last-button click logic, generated-button counting, terminal clear behavior, exact finished text, and white border styling.\" -p 5.2: \"Excluded: automated test file creation, browser execution, unrelated page content, persistence, frameworks, or server dependencies.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file affected-files-systems-data-and-interfaces -p 6.1: \"Future file: button-chain.html. Interface: direct browser clicks on visible buttons and visible document body output.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"W01 enables W02; W02 enables W03; W03 enables W04. When complete, W05 can rely on an implemented standalone HTML file ready for direct browser verification.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file implementation-approach