nly that button may append exactly one new generated button directly below it.\" -p 5.2: \"Increment a generated-button counter only when a button is appended. Attach the same last-button behavior to newly generated buttons without pre-creating extra buttons.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/02-step-add-append-handler acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Clicking the current last button once increases the visible button count by exactly one. Clicking an older non-last button does not append a new button.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/02-step-add-append-handler handoff -p 7.1: \"W03 can use the generated-button counter and current-last-button rule to identify generated button four.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/03-step-add-terminal-state instructions -p 5.1: \"Add handleTerminalGeneratedButton() for the fourth generated button branch. When generated button four is clicked as the current last button, clear the document body and render the completion message with exact text finished.\" -p 5.2: \"Do not leave the initial button, generated buttons, hidden controls, or extra visible text in the body after the terminal state.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/03-step-add-terminal-state acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"After generated button four is clicked, the body contains the completion state only, and the visible text is exactly finished in lowercase.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/03-step-add-terminal-state handoff -p 7.1: \"W04 can style the completion message element without changing its text or terminal-state creation logic.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/04-step-style-completion-border instructions -p 5.1: \"Add .completion-message styling in button-chain.html so the terminal completion element has a visible white border. Use enough border width/style and layout contrast for visual verifi