ing requirement\n    47\t\n    48\t| Test required | Rationale |\n    49\t|---|---|\n    50\t| yes | The goal changes user-facing HTML behavior and must be verified by downstream UI story W05. |\n    51\t\n    52\t§ 9.2\n    53\t`W02` — Add click behavior so only pressing the current last button appends exactly one new button directly below it.\n    54\t\n    55\t§ 9.3\n    56\t`W03` — When the fourth generated button is pressed, clear the document and render only the completion state with exact text finished.\n    57\t\n    58\t§ 9.4\n    59\t`W04` — Style the completion state with a visible white border while preserving the exact lowercase text finished.\n    60\t\n    61\t## Goal-size exception\n    62\t\n    63\t§ 11.1\n    64\t<required only when this goal has one permitted work unit>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'set -e\nPLAN=basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260810T203455Z-pilot-smoke2-isolated-plan\nSKILL=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260810T203455Z-pilot-smoke2/1.4.1/worker/planning\nU=\"$SKILL/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\"\n# Continue goal 01 with paragraph updates where section ids vary.\n\"$U\" --goal-paragraph \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file 6.1 \"Future file: button-chain.html. Interface: direct browser clicks on visible buttons and visible document body output.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-paragraph \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file 7.1 \"W01 enables W02; W02 enables W03; W03 enables W04. When complete, W05 can rely on an implemented standalone HTML file ready for direct browser verification.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Use a single source of truth for generated-button count and current-last-button eligibility. Ignore clicks on older generated buttons except the terminal click on generated button four if it is the current last button at that point.\" -p 8.2: \"After terminal state, remove prior controls so the document contains only the completion message; keep the exact text separate from styling so the border cannot alter the string assertion.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-paragraph \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file 11.1 \"Not applicable; this goal owns four work units, within the 2-10 work-unit limit.\"\n# Goal 02\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-flow current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \"This goal depends on 01-create-button-chain-file. It starts only after button-chain.html has been implemented and is available as a local browser target.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-flow why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \"The requested behavior is observable only through a direct user-facing interaction, so a separate browser story is required before the future implementation can be accepted.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-flow scope -p 5.1: \"Included: opening the implemented local HTML file, clicking through the button chain, recording append counts after each click, clicking the fourth generated button, and verifying the final text and white border.\" -p 5.2: \"Excluded: console-triggered events, direct DOM mutation, server setup, screenshots beyond useful evidence, and any code fixes during the verification step.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-paragraph \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-flow 6.1 \"Verification target: browser-rendered button-chain.html. Planning evidence targets: ui-user-stories.md, ui-story-runs/US-01.md, bugs.md if a failure is found, and the W05 testing companion.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-paragraph \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-flow 7.1 \"Depends on W01 through W04. If US-01 fails, hand off to the bug feedback loop by recording a bug row and adding investigation and fix goals before claiming completion.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-flow implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Run the cached direct-click sequence. Verify both intermediate append behavior and destructive terminal behavior because either can pass independently while the other fails.\" -p 8.2: \"If the page clears too early, appends multiple buttons, leaves old buttons after completion, changes the casing of finished, or lacks a visible white border, mark US-01 as bug found.\"\n\"$U\" --goal-paragraph \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-flow 11.1 \"Allowed single-work-unit verification goal: W05 is a standalone browser-flow proof after implementation.\"\n# Steps\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/01-step-create-initial-markup instructions -p 5.1: \"Create button-chain.html as a standalone HTML document. In the document body, render exactly one initial button and no generated buttons. Use stable text or accessible labeling so the current last button is identifiable in browser verification.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/01-step-create-initial-markup acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"A fresh load of button-chain.html displays one and only one button before any interaction. No completion message is present initially.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/01-step-create-initial-markup handoff -p 7.1: \"W02 can attach behavior to the initial button and append generated buttons beneath the existing last button.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/02-step-add-append-handler instructions -p 5.1: \"Add appendNextButton() in button-chain.html. The handler must determine whether the clicked button is the current last button; only that button may append exactly one new generated button directly below it.\" -p 5.2: \"Increment a generated-button counter only when a button is appended. Attach the same last-button behavior to newly generated buttons without pre-creating extra buttons.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/02-step-add-append-handler acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Clicking the current last button once increases the visible button count by exactly one. Clicking an older non-last button does not append a new button.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/02-step-add-append-handler handoff -p 7.1: \"W03 can use the generated-button counter and current-last-button rule to identify generated button four.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/03-step-add-terminal-state instructions -p 5.1: \"Add handleTerminalGeneratedButton() for the fourth generated button branch. When generated button four is clicked as the current last button, clear the document body and render the completion message with exact text finished.\" -p 5.2: \"Do not leave the initial button, generated buttons, hidden controls, or extra visible text in the body after the terminal state.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/03-step-add-terminal-state acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"After generated button four is clicked, the body contains the completion state only, and the visible text is exactly finished in lowercase.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/03-step-add-terminal-state handoff -p 7.1: \"W04 can style the completion message element without changing its text or terminal-state creation logic.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/04-step-style-completion-border instructions -p 5.1: \"Add .completion-message styling in button-chain.html so the terminal completion element has a visible white border. Use enough border width/style and layout contrast for visual verification.\" -p 5.2: \"Do not change the completion text while styling; the text must remain exactly finished.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/04-step-style-completion-border acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"The terminal completion message visibly shows a white border around the exact text finished.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 01-create-button-chain-file/04-step-style-completion-border handoff -p 7.1: \"W05 can verify both the exact text and visible white border in the browser.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-flow/01-step-run-ui-story instructions -p 5.1: \"Open the implemented button-chain.html in a browser after future implementation. Use the cached US-01 sequence: click the current last button until generated button four exists, then click generated button four. Record direct-click evidence and intermediate button counts.\" -p 5.2: \"Do not use console commands, JavaScript evaluation, DOM mutation, storage edits, direct API calls, or injected events to trigger the behavior.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-flow/01-step-run-ui-story acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"US-01 passes only when each append click adds exactly one button below the previous last button and the terminal click leaves only exact lowercase text finished with a visible white border.\" -p 6.2: \"Any mismatch is recorded in bugs.md with reproduction, severity, investigation goal, fix goal, retest story, and open status before implementation resumes.\"\n\"$U\" --step-section \"$PLAN\" 02-verify-button-chain-flow/01-step-run-ui-story handoff -p 7.1: \"When passed, mark US-01 passed with evidence and complete the plan. When failed, follow the bug feedback loop before acceptance.\"\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
