{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat basic-test-proof-1.4.1-20260810T203455Z-pilot-smoke2-isolated-plan/adversarial-review.md'","aggregated_output":"# Adversarial Review: Button Chain HTML Implementation Plan\n\n## Verdict\n\nRejected. The plan is close, but it is not ready to execute because the UI story run cache does not decompose the required direct browser interactions into ordered, individually observable actions and readiness checks. This weakens the exact proof needed for \"appends exactly one button below it\" on each eligible click.\n\n## Findings\n\n### AR-01 - UI story cache bundles multiple required clicks into one action\n\nStatus: open\n\nSeverity: blocking\n\nLocation: `ui-story-runs/US-01.md`\n\nThe buffered interaction sequence currently has one row: \"Click current last button four times; click the fourth generated button.\" The planning skill's UI validation contract requires caching every action in execution order, including each target/value and wait/readiness signal. For this requested task, that granularity is not optional: the acceptance proof depends on observing that each individual eligible click appends exactly one button below the current last button, then that a separate click on generated button four clears the document.\n\nRequired correction: split `US-01` into separate cached actions, at minimum:\n\n1. Fresh-load assertion: exactly one initial button and no `finished` text.\n2. Click the initial/current last button; readiness: exactly two visible buttons, generated button 1 below the initial button.\n3. Click generated button 1/current last button; readiness: exactly three visible buttons, generated button 2 below generated button 1.\n4. Click generated button 2/current last button; readiness: exactly four visible buttons, generated button 3 below generated button 2.\n5. Click generated button 3/current last button; readiness: exactly five visible buttons, generated button 4 below generated button 3, with no terminal state yet.\n6. Click generated button 4/current last button; readiness: prior controls are cleared and the body shows only exact lowercase `finished` with a visible white border.\n\nThe waits/readiness table should match those actions rather than using one terminal-only readiness check. The final verification step and testing companion already require recording intermediate counts, so this correction should align the cache with the rest of the plan rather than change scope.\n\n## Coverage Check\n\nDecomposition: covered. The plan separates initial markup, append behavior, terminal behavior, completion styling, and browser verification into W01-W05 with one owner per work unit.\n\nUI story/cache: partially covered. `US-01` exists and maps to W01-W05, but AR-01 must be fixed before approval because the cache is not action-by-action.\n\nTesting companions: covered. Each implementation/style step has a downstream browser-verification companion, and the verification step has its own companion with pass/fail criteria.\n\nBug feedback: covered. The verification goal, W05 step, testing companion, and `bugs.md` define the bug record path with investigation, fix, and retest requirements.\n\nPlanning-only constraints: covered. The plan explicitly excludes creating, opening, serving, or testing HTML during the planning proof and identifies future execution as the phase that creates and verifies `button-chain.html`.\n\n## Approval Gate\n\nDo not approve until AR-01 is resolved and a fresh review confirms the corrected cache preserves the same behavior contract.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
